{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.SelectionRules","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.SelectionRules","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.BigOperators.Ring.Finset","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.BigOperators.Group.Finset","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.LinearCombination"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SelectionRules.nonneg_sum_ne_neg_target","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SelectionRules.nonneg_sum_ne_neg_target","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SelectionRules.lean#L94-L110","doc":"**Positivity exclusion (the common cause of Δ_λ rows B and E).** A non-negative\nlinear combination of non-negative operators is non-negative, hence cannot equal a\nstrictly negative target.\n\nApplied to `Δ_λ`: on any partition where the mixed-sign target `Δ_λ < 0`, every\npositive ansatz — Frobenius co-Casimir (`1/dim_q > 0`) and the crystal/KL route\n(`Σ_w n^w_λ · X_w`, `n^w_λ ≥ 0`) — is excluded. One machine-checked selection rule\nunifies the co-Casimir wrong-sign refutation and the KL-positivity prune. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SelectionRules.id","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SelectionRules.id","kind":"def","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SelectionRules.lean#L85-L90","doc":"A trivial bar-involution (identity) witnesses that the structure is inhabited;\nthe load-bearing instance is `q ↦ q⁻¹` on the Laurent ring (built elsewhere). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SelectionRules.odd_ne_even_of_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SelectionRules.odd_ne_even_of_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SelectionRules.lean#L66-L83","doc":"**Parity orthogonality (the exclusion).** In characteristic ≠ 2 (`NoZeroDivisors`\n+ `2 ≠ 0`), a nonzero bar-**ODD** element `x` (`bar x = −x`) cannot equal any\nbar-**EVEN** element `v` (`bar v = v`): the odd and even eigenspaces of the\ninvolution meet only at `0`.\n\nApplied: the bar-odd `c₃` carrier ≠ the bar-even `−Vol(4₁)`. This is the\nscope-(b) structural reason `c₃ = −Vol(4₁)` fails — wrong bar-parity eigenspace,\nnot merely a wrong number. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SelectionRules.BarInvolution.bar_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SelectionRules.BarInvolution.bar_neg","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SelectionRules.lean#L62-L62","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SelectionRules.BarInvolution.bar_add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SelectionRules.BarInvolution.bar_add","kind":"theorem","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SelectionRules.lean#L61-L61","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SelectionRules.BarInvolution.bar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SelectionRules.BarInvolution.bar","kind":"def","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SelectionRules.lean#L60-L60","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SelectionRules.BarInvolution.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SelectionRules.BarInvolution.mk","kind":"ctor","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SelectionRules.lean#L59-L59","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SelectionRules.BarInvolution","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SelectionRules.BarInvolution","kind":"structure","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SelectionRules.lean#L56-L62","doc":"A bar-involution: an additive, negation-compatible self-map of the ring\n(the arithmetic shadow of `q ↦ q⁻¹` on the Laurent ring). Only additivity is\nneeded for the eigenspace-orthogonality argument, so we ask for no more. ","signatureChunk":0}]}